For a dependent-child residence application, the Manual says an adult child aged 21 to 24 must be totally or substantially reliant on the principal applicant and/or the principal applicant’s partner for financial support. In assessing that, immigration officers consider the whole application and relevant factors including:
- whether the child is in paid employment, and if so whether it is full time or part time and for how long;
- whether the child has any other independent means of financial support;
- whether the child is living with parents or another family member, and the extent to which other support is provided; and
- whether the child is studying, and if so whether it is full time or part time.

The Manual also says evidence of actual dependence may be required for children aged 21 to 24. If the child has done work under certain visa conditions, evidence that the work was in accordance with those visa conditions may also be required.
